      "title": "Blocks, Rescue and Always",
      "concept": "A block groups several tasks so one condition or error handler applies to all of them. A rescue section runs only when a task in the block fails, and always runs whether the block succeeded or failed, which is how you clean up after risky work.",
      "syntax": "- block:\n    - name: Risky task\n      ...\n  rescue:\n    - name: Recover\n      ...\n  always:\n    - name: Clean up\n      ...",
      "exampleCode": "- block:\n    - name: Main work\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: \"Main work done\"\n  rescue:\n    - name: Recovery\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: \"Recovered\"\n  always:\n    - name: Cleanup\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: \"Cleanup done\"",
      "exampleLanguage": "ansible",
      "mistake": "Adding ignore_errors to every task instead of grouping risky tasks in a block with a proper rescue section.",
