      "concept": "Ansible gathers facts about each host, such as its operating system, IP addresses, and memory, and stores them in the ansible_facts variable. Magic variables like inventory_hostname and groups give you the current host name and the groups it belongs to, even with fact gathering turned off.",
      "syntax": "ansible localhost -m setup\n{{ ansible_facts['os_family'] }}\n{{ inventory_hostname }}",
      "exampleCode": "- name: Show the host name\n  ansible.builtin.debug:\n    msg: \"Running on {{ inventory_hostname }}\"",
      "exampleLanguage": "ansible",
