      "title": "Why Secrets Need Vault",
      "concept": "Secrets such as database passwords and API keys must never sit in plain text in a repository, because everyone with repository access can read them. Ansible Vault encrypts files and variables with AES-256, so the secret stays in version control but only people with the vault password can read it.",
      "syntax": "ansible-vault create secrets.yml\nansible-vault view secrets.yml",
      "exampleCode": "$ ansible-vault create secrets.yml\ndb_password: hunter2   # stored encrypted on disk",
      "exampleLanguage": "ansible",
      "mistake": "Storing a password in a plain YAML file because the repository is private, forgetting that private repositories still have many readers.",
