      "slug": "ansible-vault-secrets-m2-l2",
      "title": "Vault in CI Pipelines",
      "concept": "In CI, the vault password is supplied as a protected pipeline secret and passed to the playbook with --vault-password-file or the ANSIBLE_VAULT_PASSWORD_FILE variable. The password never appears in logs or in the repository, and the pipeline job is the only place that can decrypt the secrets.",
      "syntax": "ANSIBLE_VAULT_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/vault_pass ansible-playbook site.yml",
      "exampleCode": "ANSIBLE_VAULT_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/vault_pass ansible-playbook site.yml",
      "exampleLanguage": "ansible",
      "mistake": "Echoing the vault password into a log or a debug task, where it is stored forever in the pipeline history.",
      "bug": {
       "prompt": "Find the bug: this Ansible example should demonstrate Vault in CI Pipelines, but it does not work correctly.",
       "buggyCode": "- name: Show the password\n  ansible.builtin.debug:\n    msg: \"{{ lookup('file', vault_pass_file) }}\"",
       "fixedCode": "- name: Use the password silently\n  ansible.builtin.debug:\n    msg: \"Password file loaded\"",
       "explanation": "Printing a password puts it in the CI logs where anyone with log access can read it; secrets must be used, never displayed."
      },
