      "title": "Version Pinning",
      "concept": "Version pinning records the exact version of each role and collection in requirements.yml, so a fresh install today gives the same content as a fresh install next month. Pinning is what makes a playbook that works today keep working after its dependencies release new versions.",
      "syntax": "roles:\n  - name: geerlingguy.nginx\n    version: 3.1.0",
      "exampleCode": "collections:\n  - name: community.general\n    version: 8.0.0",
      "exampleLanguage": "ansible",
      "mistake": "Pinning a role to a major version range that still allows breaking changes, instead of pinning an exact version.",
      "bug": {
       "prompt": "Find the bug: this Ansible example should demonstrate Version Pinning, but it does not work correctly.",
       "buggyCode": "roles:\n  - name: geerlingguy.nginx\n    version: \">=3.0.0\"",
       "fixedCode": "roles:\n  - name: geerlingguy.nginx\n    version: 3.1.0",
       "explanation": "A range allows a future release to change behaviour under you; an exact version is the only pin that guarantees the same content."
      },
