      "title": "Dynamic Includes and Imports",
      "concept": "The import_tasks keyword loads tasks at playbook parse time, while include_tasks loads them at run time, which means include_tasks can be used inside a loop or a condition. Imports are static and faster to validate; includes are dynamic and flexible.",
      "syntax": "- import_tasks: setup.yml\n- include_tasks: \"{{ task_file }}.yml\"",
      "exampleCode": "- name: Include tasks dynamically\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: \"{{ task_file }}.yml\"",
      "exampleLanguage": "ansible",
