      "concept": "A rolling update takes hosts out of service one batch at a time, updates them, checks they are healthy, and puts them back, so the service never goes down. The serial keyword controls the batch size, and pre_tasks and post_tasks handle the load balancer drain and rejoin.",
      "syntax": "serial: 1\npre_tasks: drain from load balancer\npost_tasks: rejoin the load balancer",
