      "title": "Validation Rules",
      "concept": "A validation block inside a variable checks the value with a condition and reports a clear error message when it fails, such as requiring an environment to be dev, staging, or prod. Validation runs before any plan, so a bad value is caught in seconds instead of halfway through an apply.",
      "syntax": "validation {\n  condition     = contains([\"dev\", \"staging\", \"prod\"], var.environment)\n  error_message = \"environment must be dev, staging, or prod.\"\n}",
      "exampleCode": "variable \"environment\" {\n  type    = string\n  default = \"dev\"\n  validation {\n    condition     = contains([\"dev\", \"staging\", \"prod\"], var.environment)\n    error_message = \"environment must be dev, staging, or prod.\"\n  }\n}\n\noutput \"environment\" {\n  value = var.environment\n}",
