      "concept": "Object types describe a value with named attributes of different types, such as object({ name = string, ports = list(number) }), and tuple types describe a fixed-length list of mixed types. Complex types make a variable's shape explicit, so a caller cannot pass a value with a missing field.",
      "syntax": "type = object({\n  name  = string\n  ports = list(number)\n})",
      "exampleCode": "variable \"server\" {\n  type = object({\n    name = string\n    port = number\n  })\n  default = {\n    name = \"web\"\n    port = 8080\n  }\n}\n\noutput \"server_name\" {\n  value = var.server.name\n}",
