      "title": "Meta-Arguments: depends_on and lifecycle",
      "concept": "Meta-arguments change how Terraform handles a resource: depends_on adds an explicit dependency, and lifecycle controls creation and destruction, such as create_before_destroy or prevent_destroy. They are used sparingly, because Terraform usually works out dependencies from the references in the configuration.",
      "syntax": "depends_on = [aws_vpc.main]\nlifecycle {\n  create_before_destroy = true\n  prevent_destroy = true\n}",
      "exampleCode": "variable \"environment\" {\n  type    = string\n  default = \"dev\"\n}\n\nlocals {\n  protect = var.environment == \"prod\"\n}\n\noutput \"protect\" {\n  value = local.protect\n}",
      "exampleLanguage": "terraform",
      "mistake": "Adding depends_on everywhere instead of referencing the resource's attributes, which hides the real dependency and makes the graph harder to follow.",
