      "title": "Tagging and Naming",
      "concept": "Tags are key-value labels on AWS resources, and a consistent tagging scheme with Name, Environment, and Owner makes every resource findable and cost-allocatable. Terraform's default_tags on the provider applies tags to every resource automatically, so none is forgotten.",
      "syntax": "provider \"aws\" {\n  default_tags {\n    tags = {\n      Environment = var.environment\n      Owner       = \"platform\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
      "exampleCode": "variable \"environment\" {\n  type    = string\n  default = \"dev\"\n}\n\nlocals {\n  tags = {\n    Environment = var.environment\n    Owner       = \"platform\"\n  }\n}\n\noutput \"tag_environment\" {\n  value = local.tags[\"Environment\"]\n}",
      "exampleLanguage": "terraform",
      "mistake": "Tagging resources by hand in each block, so one resource is inevitably missed and becomes untraceable.",
