      "concept": "Backing up a compose app means backing up its named volumes and its configuration, usually by stopping the stack, archiving the volumes, and starting it again. The compose file itself is in version control, so the backup only needs the data, not the definition.",
      "syntax": "docker compose stop\ndocker run --rm -v app-data:/data -v $(pwd):/backup alpine tar czf /backup/data.tar.gz /data\ndocker compose start",
