      "concept": "The USER instruction switches the user a container runs as, and it should be a dedicated user created in the Dockerfile, not root. Files the application writes must be owned by that user, which is why the user is created before the files are copied.",
      "syntax": "RUN adduser -D appuser\nUSER appuser",
      "exampleCode": "FROM alpine:3.19\nRUN adduser -D appuser\nUSER appuser\nRUN echo \"non-root user\" > /home/appuser/note.txt\nCMD [\"cat\", \"/home/appuser/note.txt\"]",
