      "id": "docker-security-m2-l2",
      "slug": "docker-security-m2-l2",
      "title": "Network Segmentation",
      "concept": "Network segmentation puts containers on separate networks so they can only reach the services they need, with the database on a network the web server can reach and the public internet cannot. Segmentation limits the blast radius: a compromised web container cannot reach the database network's other services.",
      "syntax": "docker network create frontend\ndocker network create backend",
      "exampleCode": "FROM alpine:3.19\nRUN echo \"segmentation limits damage\" > /segment.txt\nCMD [\"cat\", \"/segment.txt\"]",
      "exampleLanguage": "docker",
