      "concept": "A hardened container starts from a minimal pinned base, runs as a non-root user, has a read-only filesystem with a tmpfs for scratch space, drops all capabilities it does not need, and is scanned before it is pushed. Each layer of defence is small on its own, and together they make the container hard to exploit.",
      "syntax": "docker build -t myapp:1.0 .\ndocker run --read-only --cap-drop=ALL --user appuser myapp:1.0",
      "exampleCode": "FROM alpine:3.19\nRUN adduser -D appuser\nUSER appuser\nRUN echo \"hardened container\" > /home/appuser/hardened.txt\nCMD [\"cat\", \"/home/appuser/hardened.txt\"]",
