      "title": "Rollbacks",
      "concept": "A rollback returns production to the previous image, which is fast when the previous image is still in the registry with its version tag. Rollbacks work because images are immutable and versioned; a deploy that overwrites the only copy of the previous image cannot be rolled back.",
