      "title": "Image Promotion",
      "concept": "Image promotion moves an image through registries or tags as it passes stages: the image built in development is tagged for staging, and the same image is tagged for production after it passes. Promotion never rebuilds the image, so the production image is byte-for-byte the tested one.",
      "syntax": "docker tag myapp:1.0 registry/staging/myapp:1.0\ndocker tag myapp:1.0 registry/prod/myapp:1.0",
      "exampleCode": "FROM alpine:3.19\nRUN echo \"promotion moves tags\" > /promotion.txt\nCMD [\"cat\", \"/promotion.txt\"]",
      "exampleLanguage": "docker",
      "mistake": "Rebuilding the image for each stage, so staging and production run different images that were never compared.",
      "bug": {
       "prompt": "Find the bug: this Docker example should demonstrate Image Promotion, but it does not work correctly.",
       "buggyCode": "# dev builds myapp:1.0, staging rebuilds it, prod rebuilds it again",
       "fixedCode": "# one build, promoted by tagging: dev -> staging -> prod",
       "explanation": "Each rebuild can differ; promoting the same image by tagging guarantees every stage runs the identical image."
      },
