      "exampleCode": "git rebase main\ngit rebase --continue",
      "exampleLanguage": "git",
      "mistake": "Resolving a rebase conflict and running git commit instead of git rebase --continue, which creates a stray commit in the middle of the rebase.",
      "bug": {
       "prompt": "Find the bug: this Git example should demonstrate Rebase Conflicts, but it does not work correctly.",
       "buggyCode": "$ git add app.txt\n$ git commit -m \"Fix\"   # wrong: creates a new commit",
       "fixedCode": "$ git add app.txt\n$ git rebase --continue",
       "explanation": "During a rebase, the commit already exists and is being replayed; --continue resumes it, while commit creates an extra one."
      },
