      "concept": "A partial clone downloads only part of a repository's history or objects, with --filter=blob:none fetching the commits and trees but not the file contents until they are needed. It makes cloning a huge monorepo fast, because the blobs arrive on demand instead of all at once.",
      "syntax": "git clone --filter=blob:none https://example.com/monorepo.git",
      "exampleCode": "git clone --filter=blob:none https://example.com/monorepo.git",
      "exampleLanguage": "git",
      "mistake": "Using a partial clone and then running a command that needs all the blobs, so Git downloads them one by one and the command is slow.",
